{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-306955-r4531778","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Cape Malay Butter Chicken","sourcePageId":306955,"sourceRevision":"4531778","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-21T00:52:14Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Cape%20Malay%20Butter%20Chicken&oldid=4531778","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:13.004Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using cream","Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste","Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using whole chicken","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"491c99ee40c985943f38d580d9634f13c506be7764785b462f84eb7306dbf058","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chicken recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Butter chicken''' is a Cape Malay dish.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Yoghurt|yoghurt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Oil|oil]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Ginger Garlic Paste|ginger/garlic paste]]\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 1 tablespoon crushed [[Cookbook:Black Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:White Pepper|white pepper]]\n* ¼ tablespoon powdered tuj ([[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]])\n* ¼ tablespoon powdered elachi ([[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]])\n* ¼ tablespoon powdered [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 ½ tablespoon freshly pounded red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Chicken|chickens]] (split in halves)\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1 can (1 cup) tomato purée\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]]\n* Fresh [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]] sprigs\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Mix yoghurt, oil, ginger/garlic paste, half the lemon juice, and spices together. Smear this mixture over the chicken halves and allow to marinate for a few hours.\n# [[Cookbook:Grilling|Grill]] chicken over live coals or rotisserie until browned. Alternatively, lightly [[Cookbook:Pan frying|pan-fry]] and cook them.\n# Combine butter, tomato purée, and the remaining lemon juice. Mix in the leftover marinade from the chicken. Bring this mixture to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for a few minutes. Remove from the heat, and stir in the cream.\n# Place the chicken on a platter, and spread the sauce over top. [[Cookbook:Garnish|Garnish]] with mint sprigs, and serve hot.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ginger-garlic paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Cape Malay Butter Chicken","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup yoghurt","sourceText":"½ cup yoghurt","amountText":"½ cup yoghurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 tablespoon oil","sourceText":"1 tablespoon oil","amountText":"1 tablespoon oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tablespoons ginger/garlic paste","sourceText":"2 tablespoons ginger/garlic paste","amountText":"2 tablespoons ginger/garlic paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 tablespoons lemon juice","sourceText":"2 tablespoons lemon juice","amountText":"2 tablespoons lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 tablespoon crushed black pepper","sourceText":"1 tablespoon crushed black pepper","amountText":"1 tablespoon crushed black pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tablespoon white pepper","sourceText":"1 tablespoon white pepper","amountText":"1 tablespoon white pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"¼ tablespoon powdered tuj (cinnamon)","sourceText":"¼ tablespoon powdered tuj (cinnamon)","amountText":"¼ tablespoon powdered tuj (cinnamon)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"¼ tablespoon powdered elachi (cardamom)","sourceText":"¼ tablespoon powdered elachi (cardamom)","amountText":"¼ tablespoon powdered elachi (cardamom)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"¼ tablespoon powdered cloves","sourceText":"¼ tablespoon powdered cloves","amountText":"¼ tablespoon powdered cloves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 ½ tablespoon freshly pounded red chillies","sourceText":"1 ½ tablespoon freshly pounded red chillies","amountText":"1 ½ tablespoon freshly pounded red chillies","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"1 tablespoon salt","so